It was also laid down that it made no difference to their liability that the money had already been lent to the creditor before the surety bond was executed. The text of Yajnavalkya has been understood in the sense that where the suretyship is one for payment, the surety's sons are also bound to pay the debts. We are unable to hold that the present case is distinguishable on principle form the decision in
ILR 41 Mad 1071 = (Air 1919 Mad 831
) supra. The appeal is, thereofre, dismissed with costs.
